 - Edit or create a file in the /etc/audit/rules.d/ directory, ending in .rules extension, with the relevant rules to monitor login and logout events.

Example:

# printf \"
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -S all -F path=/var/log/lastlog -F perm=wa -k logins
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -S all -F path=/var/run/faillock -F perm=wa -k logins
\" >> /etc/audit/rules.d/50-login.rules

